          },
          {
            "id": "p20",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. Write and balance the equation.",
            "start": 1454,
            "end": 1488
          },
          {
            "id": "p21",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. Convert given amounts (usually in grams) to moles.",
            "start": 1489,
            "end": 1542
          },
          {
            "id": "p22",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "3. Use the mole ratio from the balanced equation to find moles of what you're looking for.",
            "start": 1543,
            "end": 1633
          },
          {
            "id": "p23",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "4. Convert back to grams if needed.",
            "start": 1634,
            "end": 1669
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The four steps correctly capture the standard sequence: balancing the reaction, converting mass to moles, applying the mole ratio, and converting moles to mass.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u5",
        "kind": "EXAMPLE",
        "label": "Worked example: Calculating mass of water formed from 8 grams of hydrogen",
        "attributes": {
          "context": "abstract_or_hypothetical",
          "treatment": "worked"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s5"
        ],
        "rationale": "Walks through a complete calculation applying the four-step stoichiometry process to determine the mass of water formed from 8 grams of hydrogen reacting with excess oxygen.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p24",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Real example**: How many grams of water can you make from 8 grams of hydrogen gas (H₂) reacting with plenty of oxygen?",
            "start": 1671,
            "end": 1791
          },
          {
            "id": "p25",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Balanced equation: 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O",
            "start": 1793,
            "end": 1827
          },
          {
            "id": "p26",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- Step 1: Convert 8 g H₂ to moles.  ",
            "start": 1829,
            "end": 1865
          },
          {
            "id": "p27",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  Molar mass of H₂ = 2 g/mol  ",
            "start": 1866,
            "end": 1896
          },
          {
            "id": "p28",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  8 g ÷ 2 g/mol = 4 moles of H₂",
            "start": 1897,
            "end": 1928
          },
          {
            "id": "p29",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- Step 2: Use the mole ratio.  ",
            "start": 1930,
            "end": 1961
          },
          {
            "id": "p30",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  From the equation: 2 moles H₂ make 2 moles H₂O  ",
            "start": 1962,
            "end": 2012
          },
          {
            "id": "p31",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  So the ratio is 2:2 (or 1:1)  ",
            "start": 2013,
            "end": 2045
          },
          {
            "id": "p32",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  4 moles H₂ will make 4 moles H₂O",
            "start": 2046,
            "end": 2080
          },
          {
            "id": "p33",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- Step 3: Convert moles of H₂O to grams.  ",
            "start": 2082,
            "end": 2124
          },
          {
            "id": "p34",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  Molar mass of H₂O = 18 g/mol  ",
            "start": 2125,
            "end": 2157
          },
          {
            "id": "p35",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "  4 moles × 18 g/mol = 72 grams of water",
            "start": 2158,
            "end": 2198
          },
